## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine subarray maxima with partition DP, requiring both maximization and reconstruction of multiple intervals. It exercises careful indexing and boundary handling.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays with a cap k
- Precomputation of maxSub for O(1) subarray maxima
- 2D DP with reconstruction pointers
- Time/space tradeoffs and edge cases (k=0, equal values)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueWithKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const maxSub = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let m = -Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      m = Math.max(m, A[r]);
      maxSub[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      let best = dp[i-1][t];
      let bestJ = -1;
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = maxSub[j-1][i-1] + dp[j-1][t-1];
        if (val > best) { best = val; bestJ = j; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = best; take[i][t] = bestJ;
    }
  }
  const res = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const j = take[i][t];
    if (j === -1) break;
    res.push([j-1, i-1]);
    i = j - 1;
    t--;
  }
  res.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], subarrays: res};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests dynamic programming on partitioning a string into numeric substrings, including numeric parsing and reconstruction, a common interview pattern.

## Key Concepts

- DP on string partitions with exact k blocks
- Efficient substring value computation and leading-zero handling
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs: O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxSumPartition(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  // val[i][j] = value of s[i..j-1]
  const val = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(n+1).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    if (s[i] === '0') { val[i][i+1] = 0; continue; }
    let cur = 0;
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      cur = cur*10 + (s.charCodeAt(j) - 48);
      val[i][j+1] = cur;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) dp[i][1] = val[0][i];
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = t-1; j < i; j++) {
        if (s[j] === '0' && i - j > 1) continue;
        const cand = dp[j][t-1] + val[j][i];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; par[i][t] = j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct cuts
  const cuts = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const j = par[i][t];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = j;
    t--;
  }
  cuts.push(0);
  cuts.reverse();
  return { sum: dp[n][k], cuts };
}
```

